# macro-metrics' FRONTEND USER STORIES, encoded from prose.
#
# Source: jemmy8oy-northstar/macro-metrics docs/user-stories-frontend.md
#         at 89053e63532166adbf2ce1894226589a498ba4db (origin/main, read 2026-09-03)
#         7 stories, 46 acceptance-criteria lines.
#
# This is the FIRST corpus in this repo not reverse-engineered from working code.
# snip-it's was read off editor.spec.ts; habits' and vocab's off DESIGN.md plus the
# routes. All three are the friendliest possible input, because a behaviour that was
# read out of a passing test is guaranteed expressible. Prose written for humans,
# before any test existed, is the honest case — and it is the case Kit will actually
# meet, since James's design starts at natural language.
#
# ⚠️ WHAT THIS FILE IS NOT: it is not "the macro-metrics corpus". It is the subset of
# 46 acceptance criteria the notation can carry. The other 30 are not omitted — every
# one is accounted for in docs/pilots/macro-metrics-prose.ledger.json, with the reason,
# and `node prose-audit.js` refuses if a single AC has no disposition. Dropping the
# hard ones and reporting a coverage percentage over what was left is exactly the
# flattering measurement this corpus exists to avoid.
#
# ── Deliberate refusals below, each a finding, none an oversight ──
# * `link:Presets/Compare/Indicators` are UNBOUND on purpose. The AC says the mini-nav
#   "contains three anchor links"; StickyNav.tsx renders three `<button onClick=…>`
#   that call scrollIntoView. A link and a button differ for keyboard, middle-click and
#   sharing, so this is a real (small) divergence, and the generator naming an unbound
#   noun is the spec constraining the app — the property Gherkin's glue removes.
# * `ratio:Errored` is UNBOUND: macro-metrics has ZERO .spec.ts files, so there is no
#   route-mock helper to bind a `given` to. Kit refuses rather than invent one.
# * The six date-range buttons are UNBOUND, and NOT because they lack names: they have
#   perfect ones ("1y" … "Max"). Nine PresetCards each render all six, so `button:Max`
#   names 9 elements and any generated locator would be ambiguous. That is finding (1)
#   in the write-up — the notation has no cardinality — arriving as a refusal.

# ── Story 1 — page loads ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

behaviour BEH-MM-LOAD-1 "The homepage renders its three sections"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-1
  actor visitor
  when opens page:MacroHome
  then sees heading:PresetRatios
  then sees heading:CustomComparison
  then sees heading:MacroIndicators
  contract all 9 preset ratio fetches fire in parallel
  contract all 3 indicator fetches fire in parallel

# The AC wants "three anchor links". The app has three buttons. Kept as the AC wrote
# it, so the refusal reports the divergence instead of the corpus absorbing it.
behaviour BEH-MM-NAV-1 "The sticky mini-nav offers the three section anchors"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-1
  actor visitor
  when opens page:MacroHome
  then sees link:Presets
  then sees link:Compare
  then sees link:Indicators

# ── Story 4 — the metric picker ────────────────────────────────────────────────

behaviour BEH-MM-PICK-0 "With nothing chosen, the compare section says what to do"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-4
  actor visitor
  when opens page:MacroHome
  then shows region:Compare "Select two metrics above to see a custom comparison"

behaviour BEH-MM-PICK-1 "Choosing only a numerator asks for the denominator"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-4
  actor visitor
  when opens page:MacroHome
  when activates combobox:Numerator
  when activates option:Gold
  then shows region:Compare "Now select a denominator"

behaviour BEH-MM-PICK-2 "Choosing both metrics renders the comparison chart"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-4
  actor visitor
  when opens page:MacroHome
  when activates combobox:Numerator
  when activates option:Gold
  when activates combobox:Denominator
  when activates option:UsCpi
  then shows region:Compare "Gold / US CPI"
  contract GET /api/metrics/ratio is fired with both metric ids

behaviour BEH-MM-SWAP-1 "The swap control is offered next to the two pickers"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-4
  actor visitor
  when opens page:MacroHome
  then sees combobox:Numerator
  then sees combobox:Denominator
  then sees button:Swap

# The picker's option list is the one collection in the whole document the notation
# CAN carry — but only as a symbol, never as an assertion. `provides` records the 11
# metrics; nothing generates a test that the dropdown offers them. Recording is not
# checking, and the gap is the finding, so it is written rather than left implicit.
behaviour BEH-MM-METRICS-1 "Eleven metrics are comparable"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-4
  actor visitor
  provides combobox:Numerator.options = UK House Prices, US House Prices, UK Wages, US Wages, UK CPI, US CPI, Gold, Oil, FTSE 100, S&P 500, Bitcoin

# ── Story 5 — the comparison chart's failure path ──────────────────────────────

behaviour BEH-MM-ERR-1 "A failed comparison fetch says so and offers a retry"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-5
  actor visitor
  given ratio:Errored
  when opens page:MacroHome
  then shows region:Compare "Could not load data."
  then sees button:TryAgain
  contract the Try again button re-fires only that card's fetch

# ── Story 6 / 7 — per-card failure ─────────────────────────────────────────────

behaviour BEH-MM-IND-ERR-1 "A failed indicator card says it is unavailable"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-6
  actor visitor
  given ratio:Errored
  when opens page:MacroHome
  then shows region:Indicators "Unavailable"

# Story 7's universal ("an error on one card does not affect others") has no shape in
# the notation. Its testable INSTANCE does: name one failing card and one working one.
# The instance is written; the universal is recorded in the ledger as inexpressible.
behaviour BEH-MM-ISOLATION-1 "One card's error leaves the others readable"
  source defined docs/user-stories-frontend.md#story-7
  actor visitor
  given ratio:OneErrored
  when opens page:MacroHome
  then shows region:Presets "Could not load data."
  then shows region:Indicators "Unavailable"
  contract every other card still renders its value
